    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today's slate leaning heavily on elite sprint speed and top-of-the-order aggression. Our premier play is **Trea Turner** (62.44), whose profile against Manaea is bolstered significantly by his leadoff spot and favorable wind conditions. Similarly, **Carson Benge** (62.17) offers an elite floor as our leadoff utility option; despite facing a tough assignment in Nola, his projection benefits from the wind and top-order efficiency. **Caleb Durbin** (64.36) anchors our infield scoring today, leveraging a favorable park and solid platoon positioning against Yesavage, making him our highest-rated starter despite hitting seventh. We are also closely tracking **Kyle Schwarber** (60.51) and **Nelson Velazquez** (54.86); the former remains a high-upside play due to his elite xwOBA, while the latter is a primary beneficiary of a positive platoon split, despite the moderate challenge presented by Cameron.\n\nStrategic depth remains a concern as we balance game caps. The most difficult bench decisions were effectively mitigated by scheduled team off-days for heavy hitters like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. Among the active roster, **Josh Smith** (43.26) and **Lars Nootbaar** (44.65) hovered closest to the cutoff; **Josh Smith** provides a necessary platoon edge against Ryan, but his low raw projection makes him a high-risk start if we need to preserve caps. We are monitoring **Casey Schmitt** and **Lars Nootbaar** closely due to the \"Lineup Pending\" status; if they fall out of the projected order, their efficiency scores will drop, forcing us to lean on depth options like **Colt Keith** or **Luke Raley** to maintain 5x5 coverage. \n\nFinally, a note on prospect development: while **Hyeseong Kim** remains a high-ceiling asset, he is currently buried in the minors with Oklahoma City and unavailable for selection. We continue to hold **Zac Veen**, **Rece Hinds**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, **Jose Fernandez**, and **Pedro Ramirez** in developmental slots, waiting for the right platoon or injury-fill opportunity to integrate them into the daily rotation. For today, the focus remains on leveraging **Trea Turner** and **Caleb Durbin** to capitalize on stolen base potential and run production against a mix of vulnerable pitching staffs.",
